Body:
@sam-huckaby thank you so much for helping with this! Some feedback:
- we actually want all tooltips to be dark mode looking, even on light mode; it's a stylistic choice
- let's reduce the contrast between the background shades, "stronger" should be lighter

@rekram1-node Thanks for the response. Yep, I tried switching modes, it didn't make a difference.

I asked here because that's the only related issue I could find, and the fact that no one else opened an issue about this made me doubt that maybe it's just me doing something wrong (I'm a new OpenCode user).

But regardless, I opened a new issue specifically for Vertex - https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/9894

It's because the nixpkgs hash in the repo reference a snapshot with issues on darwin, make your opencode integration follow  the current: 

```nix
    opencode.url = "github:anomalyco/opencode";
    opencode.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";
```
